Package: HyperCom
Title: A Hypergraph Method to Understand Cell-Cell Communication
Version: 0.3.1
Authors@R: 
    c(person("Justin", "Moy", , "jmmoy@bu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7566-2215")),
    person("Pawel", "Przytycki", , "pawel@bu.edu", role = c("aut", "ths"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3360-6936")))
Description: Infers cell-resolved cell-cell communication from single-cell
    transcriptomics data without aggregating cells by type (Moy and Przytycki
    (2026) <doi:10.64898/2026.09.30.755742>). HyperCom builds a hypergraph from
    known ligand-receptor interactions and the expression of those ligands and
    receptors in individual cells, diffuses over it by a random walk with
    restart, and scores each cell on a continuous spectrum from sender to
    receiver for each ligand-receptor pair. It then ranks ligand-receptor pairs
    by communication over the whole dataset, optionally favoring pairs whose
    cells concentrate in some conditions, with optional permutation p-values.
    It scales to about 100,000 cells per sample on a 64 GB computer. Input is
    a counts matrix with cell metadata, or a
    'Seurat' or 'SingleCellExperiment' object; 'CellChat' ligand-receptor
    databases for human and mouse are included.
URL: https://github.com/pawelab/HyperCom
